ll!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"IV.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Perhaps you\'d like to buy a flower?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But I could never sell.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"If you would like to borrow\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Until the daffodil\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Unties her yellow bonnet\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Beneath the village door,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Until the bees, from clover rows\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Their hock and sherry draw,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Why, I will lend until just then,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But not an hour more!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"V.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The pedigree of honey\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Does not concern the bee;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A clover, any time, to him\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Is aristocracy.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"VI.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A SERVICE OF SONG.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Some keep the Sabbath going to church;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I keep it staying at home,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"With a bobolink for a chorister,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And an orchard for a dome.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Some keep the Sabbath in surplice;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I just wear my wings,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And instead of tolling the bell for church,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Our little sexton sings.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"God preaches, — a noted clergyman, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And the sermon is never long;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"So instead of getting to heaven at last,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I\'m going all along!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"VII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The bee is not afraid of me,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I know the butterfly;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The pretty people in the woods\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Receive me cordially.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The brooks laugh louder when I come,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The breezes madder play.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Wherefore, mine eyes, thy silver mists?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Wherefore, O summer\'s day?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"VIII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"SUMMER\'S ARMIES.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Some rainbow coming from the fair!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Some vision of the world Cashmere\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I confidently see!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Or else a peacock\'s purple train,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Feather by feather, on the plain\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Fritters itself away!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The dreamy butterflies bestir,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Lethargic pools resume the whir\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Of last year\'s sundered tune.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"From some old fortress on the sun\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Baronial bees march, one by one,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"In murmuring platoon!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The robins stand as thick to-day\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"As flakes of snow stood yesterday,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"On fence and roof and twig.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The orchis binds her feather on\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"For her old lover, Don the Sun,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Revisiting the bog!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Without commander, countless, still,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The regiment of wood and hill\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"In bright detachment stand.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Behold! Whose multitudes are these?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The children of whose turbaned seas,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Or what Circassian land?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"IX.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"THE GRASS.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The grass so little has to do, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A sphere of simple green,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"With only butterflies to brood,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And bees to entertain,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And stir all day to pretty tunes\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The breezes fetch along,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And hold the sunshine in its lap\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And bow to everything;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And thread the dews all night, like pearls,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And make itself so fine, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A duchess were too common\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"For such a noticing.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And even when it dies, to pass\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"In odors so divine,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"As lowly spices gone to sleep,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Or amulets of pine.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And then to dwell in sovereign barns,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And dream the days away, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The grass so little has to do,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I wish I were the hay!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"X.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A little road not made of man,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Enabled of the eye,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Accessible to thill of bee,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Or cart of butterfly.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"If town it have, beyond itself,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"\'T is that I cannot say;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I only sigh, — no vehicle\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Bears me along that way.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XI.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"SUMMER SHOWER.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A drop fell on the apple tree,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Another on the roof;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A half a dozen kissed the eaves,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And made the gables laugh.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A few went out to help the brook,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That went to help the sea.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Myself conjectured, Were they pearls,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"What necklaces could be!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The dust replaced in hoisted roads,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The birds jocoser sung;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The sunshine threw his hat away,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The orchards spangles hung.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The breezes brought dejected lutes,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And bathed them in the glee;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The East put out a single flag,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And signed the fete away.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"PSALM OF THE DAY.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A something in a summer\'s day,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"As slow her flambeaux burn away,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Which solemnizes me.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A something in a summer\'s noon, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"An azure depth, a wordless tune,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Transcending ecstasy.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And still within a summer\'s night\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A something so transporting bright,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I clap my hands to see;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Then veil my too inspecting face,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Lest such a subtle, shimmering grace\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Flutter too far for me.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The wizard-fingers never rest,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The purple brook within the breast\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Still chafes its narrow bed;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Still rears the East her amber flag,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Guides still the sun along the crag\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"His caravan of red,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Like flowers that heard the tale of dews,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But never deemed the dripping prize\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Awaited their low brows;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Or bees, that thought the summer\'s name\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Some rumor of delirium\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"No summer could for them;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Or Arctic creature, dimly stirred\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"By tropic hint, — some travelled bird\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Imported to the wood;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Or wind\'s bright signal to the ear,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Making that homely and severe,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Contented, known, before\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The heaven unexpected came,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"To lives that thought their worshipping\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A too presumptuous psalm.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XIII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"THE SEA OF SUNSET.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"This is the land the sunset washes,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"These are the banks of the Yellow Sea;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Where it rose, or whither it rushes,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"These are the western mystery!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Night after night her purple traffic\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Strews the landing with opal bales;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Merchantmen poise upon horizons,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Dip, and vanish with fairy sails.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XIV.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"PURPLE CLOVER.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"There is a flower that bees prefer,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And butterflies desire;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"To gain the purple democrat\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The humming-birds aspire.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And whatsoever insect pass,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A honey bears away\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Proportioned to his several dearth\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And her capacity.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Her face is rounder than the moon,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And ruddier than the gown\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Of orchis in the pasture,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Or rhododendron worn.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"She doth not wait for June;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Before the world is green\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Her sturdy little countenance\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Against the wind is seen,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Contending with the grass,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Near kinsman to herself,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"For privilege of sod and sun,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Sweet litigants for life.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And when the hills are full,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And newer fashions blow,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Doth not retract a single spice\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"For pang of jealousy.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Her public is the noon,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Her providence the sun,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Her progress by the bee proclaimed\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"In sovereign, swerveless tune.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The bravest of the host,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Surrendering the last,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Nor even of defeat aware\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"When cancelled by the frost.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XV.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"THE BEE.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Like trains of cars on tracks of plush\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I hear the level bee:\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A jar across the flowers goes,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Their velvet masonry\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Withstands until the sweet assault\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Their chivalry consumes,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"While he, victorious, tilts away\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"To vanquish other blooms.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"His feet are shod with gauze,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"His helmet is of gold;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"His breast, a single onyx\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"With chrysoprase, inlaid.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"His labor is a chant,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"His idleness a tune;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Oh, for a bee\'s experience\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Of clovers and of noon!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XVI.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Presentiment is that long shadow on the lawn\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Indicative that suns go down;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The notice to the startled grass\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That darkness is about to pass.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XVII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"As children bid the guest good-night,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And then reluctant turn,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"My flowers raise their pretty lips,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Then put their nightgowns on.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"As children caper when they wake,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Merry that it is morn,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"My flowers from a hundred cribs\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Will peep, and prance again.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XVIII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Angels in the early morning\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"May be seen the dews among,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Stooping, plucking, smiling, flying:\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Do the buds to them belong?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Angels when the sun is hottest\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"May be seen the sands among,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Stooping, plucking, sighing, flying;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Parched the flowers they bear along.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XIX.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"So bashful when I spied her,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"So pretty, so ashamed!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"So hidden in her leaflets,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Lest anybody find;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"So breathless till I passed her,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"So helpless when I turned\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And bore her, struggling, blushing,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Her simple haunts beyond!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"For whom I robbed the dingle,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"For whom betrayed the dell,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Many will doubtless ask me,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But I shall never tell!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XX.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"TWO WORLDS.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"It makes no difference abroad,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The seasons fit the same,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The mornings blossom into noons,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And split their pods of flame.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Wild-flowers kindle in the woods,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The brooks brag all the day;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"No blackbird bates his jargoning\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"For passing Calvary.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Auto-da-fe and judgment\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Are nothing to the bee;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"His separation from his rose\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"To him seems misery.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXI.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"THE MOUNTAIN.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The mountain sat upon the plain\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"In his eternal chair,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"His observation omnifold,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"His inquest everywhere.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The seasons prayed around his knees,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Like children round a sire:\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Grandfather of the days is he,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Of dawn the ancestor.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A DAY.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I\'ll tell you how the sun rose, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A ribbon at a time.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The steeples swam in amethyst,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The news like squirrels ran.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The hills untied their bonnets,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The bobolinks begun.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Then I said softly to myself,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"\\\"That must have been the sun!\\\"\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"* * *\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But how he set, I know not.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"There seemed a purple stile\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Which little yellow boys and girls\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Were climbing all the while\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Till when they reached the other side,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A dominie in gray\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Put gently up the evening bars,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And led the flock away.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXIII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The butterfly\'s assumption-gown,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"In chrysoprase apartments hung,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"This afternoon put on.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"How condescending to descend,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And be of buttercups the friend\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"In a New England town!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXIV.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"THE WIND.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Of all the sounds despatched abroad,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"There\'s not a charge to me\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Like that old measure in the boughs,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That phraseless melody\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The wind does, working like a hand\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Whose fingers brush the sky,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Then quiver down, with tufts of tune\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Permitted gods and me.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"When winds go round and round in bands,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And thrum upon the door,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And birds take places overhead,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"To bear them orchestra,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I crave him grace, of summer boughs,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"If such an outcast be,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"He never heard that fleshless chant\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Rise solemn in the tree,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"As if some caravan of sound\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"On deserts, in the sky,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Had broken rank,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Then knit, and passed\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"In seamless company.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXV.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"DEATH AND LIFE.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Apparently with no surprise\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"To any happy flower,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The frost beheads it at its play\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"In accidental power.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The blond assassin passes on,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The sun proceeds unmoved\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"To measure off another day\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"For an approving God.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXVI.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"\'T was later when the summer went\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Than when the cricket came,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And yet we knew that gentle clock\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Meant nought but going home.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"\'T was sooner when the cricket went\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Than when the winter came,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Yet that pathetic pendulum\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Keeps esoteric time.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXVII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"INDIAN SUMMER.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"These are the days when birds come back,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A very few, a bird or two,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"To take a backward look.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"These are the days when skies put on\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The old, old sophistries of June, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A blue and gold mistake.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Oh, fraud that cannot cheat the bee,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Almost thy plausibility\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Induces my belief,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Till ranks of seeds their witness bear,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And softly through the altered air\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Hurries a timid leaf!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Oh, sacrament of summer days,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Oh, last communion in the haze,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Permit a child to join,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Thy sacred emblems to partake,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Thy consecrated bread to break,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Taste thine immortal wine!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXVIII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"AUTUMN.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The morns are meeker than they were,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The nuts are getting brown;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The berry\'s cheek is plumper,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The rose is out of town.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The maple wears a gayer scarf,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The field a scarlet gown.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Lest I should be old-fashioned,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I\'ll put a trinket on.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXIX.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"BECLOUDED.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The sky is low, the clouds are mean,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A travelling flake of snow\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Across a barn or through a rut\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Debates if it will go.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A narrow wind complains all day\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"How some one treated him;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Nature, like us, is sometimes caught\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Without her diadem.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXX.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"THE HEMLOCK.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I think the hemlock likes to stand\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Upon a marge of snow;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"It suits his own austerity,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And satisfies an awe\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That men must slake in wilderness,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Or in the desert cloy, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"An instinct for the hoar, the bald,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Lapland\'s necessity.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The hemlock\'s nature thrives on cold;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The gnash of northern winds\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Is sweetest nutriment to him,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"His best Norwegian wines.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"To satin races he is nought;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But children on the Don\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Beneath his tabernacles play,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And Dnieper wrestlers run.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXXI.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"There\'s a certain slant of light,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"On winter afternoons,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That oppresses, like the weight\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Of cathedral tunes.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Heavenly hurt it gives us;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"We can find no scar,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But internal difference\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Where the meanings are.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"None may teach it anything,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"\'T is the seal, despair, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"An imperial affliction\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Sent us of the air.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"When it comes, the landscape listens,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Shadows hold their breath;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"When it goes, \'t is like the distance\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"On the look of death.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"IV. TIME AND ETERNITY.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"One dignity delays for all,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"One mitred afternoon.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"None can avoid this purple,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"None evade this crown.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Coach it insures, and footmen,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Chamber and state and throng;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Bells, also, in the village,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"As we ride grand along.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"What dignified attendants,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"What service when we pause!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"How loyally at parting\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Their hundred hats they raise!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"How pomp surpassing ermine,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"When simple you and I\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Present our meek escutcheon,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And claim the rank to die!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"II.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"TOO LATE.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Delayed till she had ceased to know,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Delayed till in its vest of snow\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Her loving bosom lay.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"An hour behind the fleeting breath,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Later by just an hour than death, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Oh, lagging yesterday!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Could she have guessed that it would be;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Could but a crier of the glee\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Have climbed the distant hill;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Had not the bliss so slow a pace, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Who knows but this surrendered face\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Were undefeated still?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Oh, if there may departing be\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Any forgot by victory\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"In her imperial round,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Show them this meek apparelled thing,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That could not stop to be a king,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Doubtful if it be crowned!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"III.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"ASTRA CASTRA.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Departed to the judgment,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A mighty afternoon;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Great clouds like ushers leaning,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Creation looking on.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The flesh surrendered, cancelled,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The bodiless begun;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Two worlds, like audiences, disperse\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And leave the soul alone.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"IV.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Safe in their alabaster chambers,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Untouched by morning and untouched by noon,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Sleep the meek members of the resurrection,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Rafter of satin, and roof of stone.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Light laughs the breeze in her castle of sunshine;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Babbles the bee in a stolid ear;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Pipe the sweet birds in ignorant cadence, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Ah, what sagacity perished here!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Grand go the years in the crescent above them;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Worlds scoop their arcs, and firmaments row,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Diadems drop and Doges surrender,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Soundless as dots on a disk of snow.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"V.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"On this long storm the rainbow rose,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"On this late morn the sun;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The clouds, like listless elephants,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Horizons straggled down.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The birds rose smiling in their nests,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The gales indeed were done;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Alas! how heedless were the eyes\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"On whom the summer shone!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The quiet nonchalance of death\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"No daybreak can bestir;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The slow archangel\'s syllables\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Must awaken her.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"VI.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"FROM THE CHRYSALIS.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"My cocoon tightens, colors tease,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I\'m feeling for the air;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A dim capacity for wings\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Degrades the dress I wear.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A power of butterfly must be\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The aptitude to fly,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Meadows of majesty concedes\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And easy sweeps of sky.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"So I must baffle at the hint\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And cipher at the sign,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And make much blunder, if at last\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I take the clew divine.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"VII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"SETTING SAIL.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Exultation is the going\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Of an inland soul to sea, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Past the houses, past the headlands,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Into deep eternity!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Bred as we, among the mountains,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Can the sailor understand\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The divine intoxication\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Of the first league out from land?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"VIII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Look back on time with kindly eyes,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"He doubtless did his best;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"How softly sinks his trembling sun\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"In human nature\'s west!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"IX.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A train went through a burial gate,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A bird broke forth and sang,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And trilled, and quivered, and shook his throat\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Till all the churchyard rang;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And then adjusted his little notes,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And bowed and sang again.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Doubtless, he thought it meet of him\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"To say good-by to men.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"X.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I died for beauty, but was scarce\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Adjusted in the tomb,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"When one who died for truth was lain\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"In an adjoining room.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"He questioned softly why I failed?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"\\\"For beauty,\\\" I replied.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"\\\"And I for truth, — the two are one;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"We brethren are,\\\" he said.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And so, as kinsmen met a night,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"We talked between the rooms,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Until the moss had reached our lips,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And covered up our names.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XI.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"\\\"TROUBLED ABOUT MANY THINGS.\\\"\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"How many times these low feet staggered,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Only the soldered mouth can tell;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Try! can you stir the awful rivet?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Try! can you lift the hasps of steel?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Stroke the cool forehead, hot so often,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Lift, if you can, the listless hair;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Handle the adamantine fingers\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Never a thimble more shall wear.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Buzz the dull flies on the chamber window;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Brave shines the sun through the freckled pane;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Fearless the cobweb swings from the ceiling —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Indolent housewife, in daisies lain!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"REAL.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I like a look of agony,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Because I know it \'s true;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Men do not sham convulsion,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Nor simulate a throe.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The eyes glaze once, and that is death.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Impossible to feign\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The beads upon the forehead\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"By homely anguish strung.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XIII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"THE FUNERAL.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That short, potential stir\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That each can make but once,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That bustle so illustrious\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"\'T is almost consequence,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Is the eclat of death.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Oh, thou unknown renown\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That not a beggar would accept,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Had he the power to spurn!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XIV.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I went to thank her,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But she slept;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Her bed a funnelled stone,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"With nosegays at the head and foot,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That travellers had thrown,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Who went to thank her;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But she slept.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"\'T was short to cross the sea\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"To look upon her like, alive,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But turning back \'t was slow.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XV.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I\'ve seen a dying eye\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Run round and round a room\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"In search of something, as it seemed,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Then cloudier become;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And then, obscure with fog,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And then be soldered down,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Without disclosing what it be,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"\'T were blessed to have seen.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XVI.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"REFUGE.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The clouds their backs together laid,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The north begun to push,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The forests galloped till they fell,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The lightning skipped like mice;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The thunder crumbled like a stuff —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"How good to be safe in tombs,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Where nature\'s temper cannot reach,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Nor vengeance ever comes!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XVII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I never saw a moor,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I never saw the sea;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Yet know I how the heather looks,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And what a wave must be.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I never spoke with God,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Nor visited in heaven;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Yet certain am I of the spot\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"As if the chart were given.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XVIII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"PLAYMATES.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"God permits industrious angels\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Afternoons to play.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I met one, — forgot my school-mates,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"All, for him, straightway.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"God calls home the angels promptly\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"At the setting sun;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I missed mine. How dreary marbles,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"After playing Crown!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XIX.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"To know just how he suffered would be dear;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"To know if any human eyes were near\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"To whom he could intrust his wavering gaze,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Until it settled firm on Paradise.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"To know if he was patient, part content,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Was dying as he thought, or different;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Was it a pleasant day to die,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And did the sunshine face his way?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"What was his furthest mind, of home, or God,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Or what the distant say\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"At news that he ceased human nature\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"On such a day?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And wishes, had he any?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Just his sigh, accented,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Had been legible to me.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And was he confident until\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Ill fluttered out in everlasting well?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And if he spoke, what name was best,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"What first,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"What one broke off with\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"At the drowsiest?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Was he afraid, or tranquil?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Might he know\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"How conscious consciousness could grow,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Till love that was, and love too blest to be,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Meet — and the junction be Eternity?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XX.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The last night that she lived,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"It was a common night,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Except the dying; this to us\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Made nature different.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"We noticed smallest things, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Things overlooked before,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"By this great light upon our minds\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Italicized, as \'t were.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That others could exist\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"While she must finish quite,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A jealousy for her arose\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"So nearly infinite.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"We waited while she passed;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"It was a narrow time,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Too jostled were our souls to speak,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"At length the notice came.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"She mentioned, and forgot;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Then lightly as a reed\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Bent to the water, shivered scarce,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Consented, and was dead.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And we, we placed the hair,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And drew the head erect;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And then an awful leisure was,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Our faith to regulate.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXI.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"THE FIRST LESSON.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Not in this world to see his face\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Sounds long, until I read the place\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Where this is said to be\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But just the primer to a life\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Unopened, rare, upon the shelf,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Clasped yet to him and me.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And yet, my primer suits me so\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I would not choose a book to know\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Than that, be sweeter wise;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Might some one else so learned be,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And leave me just my A B C,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Himself could have the skies.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The bustle in a house\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The morning after death\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Is solemnest of industries\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Enacted upon earth, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The sweeping up the heart,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And putting love away\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"We shall not want to use again\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Until eternity.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXIII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I reason, earth is short,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And anguish absolute,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And many hurt;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But what of that?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I reason, we could die:\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The best vitality\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Cannot excel decay;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But what of that?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I reason that in heaven\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Somehow, it will be even,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Some new equation given;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But what of that?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXIV.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Afraid? Of whom am I afraid?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Not death; for who is he?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The porter of my father\'s lodge\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"As much abasheth me.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Of life? \'T were odd I fear a thing\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That comprehendeth me\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"In one or more existences\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"At Deity\'s decree.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Of resurrection? Is the east\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Afraid to trust the morn\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"With her fastidious forehead?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"As soon impeach my crown!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXV.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"DYING.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The sun kept setting, setting still;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"No hue of afternoon\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Upon the village I perceived, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"From house to house \'t was noon.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The dusk kept dropping, dropping still;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"No dew upon the grass,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But only on my forehead stopped,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And wandered in my face.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"My feet kept drowsing, drowsing still,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"My fingers were awake;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Yet why so little sound myself\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Unto my seeming make?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"How well I knew the light before!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I could not see it now.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"\'T is dying, I am doing; but\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I\'m not afraid to know.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXVI.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Two swimmers wrestled on the spar\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Until the morning sun,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"When one turned smiling to the land.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"O God, the other one!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The stray ships passing spied a face\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Upon the waters borne,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"With eyes in death still begging raised,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And hands beseeching thrown.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXVII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"THE CHARIOT.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Because I could not stop for Death,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"He kindly stopped for me;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The carriage held but just ourselves\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And Immortality.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"We slowly drove, he knew no haste,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And I had put away\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"My labor, and my leisure too,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"For his civility.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"We passed the school where children played,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Their lessons scarcely done;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"We passed the fields of gazing grain,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"We passed the setting sun.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"We paused before a house that seemed\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A swelling of the ground;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The roof was scarcely visible,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The cornice but a mound.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Since then \'t is centuries; but each\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Feels shorter than the day\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I first surmised the horses\' heads\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Were toward eternity.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXVIII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"She went as quiet as the dew\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"From a familiar flower.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Not like the dew did she return\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"At the accustomed hour!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"She dropt as softly as a star\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"From out my summer\'s eve;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Less skilful than Leverrier\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"It\'s sorer to believe!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXIX.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"RESURGAM.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"At last to be identified!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"At last, the lamps upon thy side,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The rest of life to see!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Past midnight, past the morning star!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Past sunrise! Ah! what leagues there are\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Between our feet and day!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXX.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Except to heaven, she is nought;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Except for angels, lone;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Except to some wide-wandering bee,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A flower superfluous blown;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Except for winds, provincial;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Except by butterflies,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Unnoticed as a single dew\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That on the acre lies.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The smallest housewife in the grass,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Yet take her from the lawn,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And somebody has lost the face\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That made existence home!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXXI.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Death is a dialogue between\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The spirit and the dust.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"\\\"Dissolve,\\\" says Death. The Spirit, \\\"Sir,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I have another trust.\\\"\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Death doubts it, argues from the ground.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The Spirit turns away,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Just laying off, for evidence,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"An overcoat of clay.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXXII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"It was too late for man,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But early yet for God;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Creation impotent to help,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But prayer remained our side.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"How excellent the heaven,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"When earth cannot be had;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"How hospitable, then, the face\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Of our old neighbor, God!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXXIII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"ALONG THE POTOMAC.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"When I was small, a woman died.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"To-day her only boy\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Went up from the Potomac,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"His face all victory,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"To look at her; how slowly\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The seasons must have turned\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Till bullets clipt an angle,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And he passed quickly round!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"If pride shall be in Paradise\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I never can decide;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Of their imperial conduct,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"No person testified.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But proud in apparition,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That woman and her boy\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Pass back and forth before my brain,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"As ever in the sky.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXXIV.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The daisy follows soft the sun,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And when his golden walk is done,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Sits shyly at his feet.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"He, waking, finds the flower near.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"\\\"Wherefore, marauder, art thou here?\\\"\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"\\\"Because, sir, love is sweet!\\\"\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"We are the flower, Thou the sun!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Forgive us, if as days decline,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"We nearer steal to Thee, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Enamoured of the parting west,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The peace, the flight, the amethyst,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Night\'s possibility!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXXV.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"EMANCIPATION.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"No rack can torture me,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"My soul\'s at liberty\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Behind this mortal bone\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"There knits a bolder one\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"You cannot prick with saw,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Nor rend with scymitar.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Two bodies therefore be;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Bind one, and one will flee.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The eagle of his nest\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"No easier divest\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And gain the sky,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Than mayest thou,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Except thyself may be\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Thine enemy;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Captivity is consciousness,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"So\'s liberty.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXXVI.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"LOST.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I lost a world the other day.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Has anybody found?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"You\'ll know it by the row of stars\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Around its forehead bound.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A rich man might not notice it;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Yet to my frugal eye\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Of more esteem than ducats.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Oh, find it, sir, for me!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXXVII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"If I shouldn\'t be alive\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"When the robins come,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Give the one in red cravat\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A memorial crumb.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"If I couldn\'t thank you,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Being just asleep,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"You will know I\'m trying\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"With my granite lip!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXXVIII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Sleep is supposed to be,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"By souls of sanity,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The shutting of the eye.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Sleep is the station grand\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Down which on either hand\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The hosts of witness stand!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Morn is supposed to be,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"By people of degree,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The breaking of the day.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Morning has not occurred!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That shall aurora be\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"East of eternity;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"One with the banner gay,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"One in the red array, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That is the break of day.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXXIX.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I shall know why, when time is over,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And I have ceased to wonder why;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Christ will explain each separate anguish\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"In the fair schoolroom of the sky.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"He will tell me what Peter promised,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And I, for wonder at his woe,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I shall forget the drop of anguish\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That scalds me now, that scalds me now.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XL.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I never lost as much but twice,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And that was in the sod;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Twice have I stood a beggar\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Before the door of God!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Angels, twice descending,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Reimbursed my store.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Burglar, banker, father,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I am poor once more!\"}]},{\"title\":\"Second Series\",\"blocks\":[{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Edited by two of her friends\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"MABEL LOOMIS TODD and T.W. HIGGINSON\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"PREFACE\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The eagerness with which the first volume of Emily Dickinson\'s\\npoems has been read shows very clearly that all our alleged modern\\nartificiality does not prevent a prompt appreciation of the\\nqualities of directness and simplicity in approaching the greatest\\nthemes,—life and love and death. That \\\"irresistible needle-touch,\\\"\\nas one of her best critics has called it, piercing at once the very\\ncore of a thought, has found a response as wide and sympathetic as\\nit has been unexpected even to those who knew best her compelling\\npower. This second volume, while open to the same criticism as to\\nform with its predecessor, shows also the same shining beauties.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Although Emily Dickinson had been in the habit of sending\\noccasional poems to friends and correspondents, the full extent of\\nher writing was by no means imagined by them. Her friend \\\"H.H.\\\"\\nmust at least have suspected it, for in a letter dated 5th\\nSeptember, 1884, she wrote:—\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"MY DEAR FRIEND,— What portfolios full of verses\\nyou must have! It is a cruel wrong to your \\\"day and\\ngeneration\\\" that you will not give them light.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"If such a thing should happen as that I should outlive\\nyou, I wish you would make me your literary legatee\\nand executor. Surely after you are what is called\\n\\\"dead\\\" you will be willing that the poor ghosts you\\nhave left behind should be cheered and pleased by your\\nverses, will you not? You ought to be. I do not think\\nwe have a right to withhold from the world a word or\\na thought any more than a deed which might help a\\nsingle soul. . . .\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Truly yours,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"HELEN JACKSON.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The \\\"portfolios\\\" were found, shortly after Emily Dickinson\'s death,\\nby her sister and only surviving housemate. Most of the poems had\\nbeen carefully copied on sheets of note-paper, and tied in little\\nfascicules, each of six or eight sheets. While many of them bear\\nevidence of having been thrown off at white heat, still more had\\nreceived thoughtful revision. There is the frequent addition of\\nrather perplexing foot-notes, affording large choice of words and\\nphrases. And in the copies which she sent to friends, sometimes one\\nform, sometimes another, is found to have been used. Without\\nimportant exception, her friends have generously placed at the\\ndisposal of the Editors any poems they had received from her; and\\nthese have given the obvious advantage of comparison among several\\nrenderings of the same verse.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"To what further rigorous pruning her verses would have been\\nsubjected had she published them herself, we cannot know. They\\nshould be regarded in many cases as merely the first strong and\\nsuggestive sketches of an artist, intended to be embodied at some\\ntime in the finished picture.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Emily Dickinson appears to have written her first poems in the\\nwinter of 1862. In a letter to one of the present Editors the\\nApril following, she says, \\\"I made no verse, but one or two, until\\nthis winter.\\\"\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The handwriting was at first somewhat like the delicate, running\\nItalian hand of our elder gentlewomen; but as she advanced in\\nbreadth of thought, it grew bolder and more abrupt, until in her\\nlatest years each letter stood distinct and separate from its\\nfellows. In most of her poems, particularly the later ones,\\neverything by way of punctuation was discarded, except numerous\\ndashes; and all important words began with capitals. The effect of\\na page of her more recent manuscript is exceedingly quaint and\\nstrong. The fac-simile given in the present volume is from one of\\nthe earlier transition periods. Although there is nowhere a date,\\nthe handwriting makes it possible to arrange the poems with general\\nchronologic accuracy.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"As a rule, the verses were without titles; but \\\"A Country Burial,\\\"\\n\\\"A Thunder-Storm,\\\" \\\"The Humming-Bird,\\\" and a few others were named\\nby their author, frequently at the end,—sometimes only in the\\naccompanying note, if sent to a friend.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The variation of readings, with the fact that she often wrote in\\npencil and not always clearly, have at times thrown a good deal of\\nresponsibility upon her Editors. But all interference not\\nabsolutely inevitable has been avoided. The very roughness of her\\nrendering is part of herself, and not lightly to be touched; for it\\nseems in many cases that she intentionally avoided the smoother and\\nmore usual rhymes.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Like impressionist pictures, or Wagner\'s rugged music, the very\\nabsence of conventional form challenges attention. In Emily\\nDickinson\'s exacting hands, the especial, intrinsic fitness of a\\nparticular order of words might not be sacrificed to anything\\nvirtually extrinsic; and her verses all show a strange cadence of\\ninner rhythmical music. Lines are always daringly constructed, and\\nthe \\\"thought-rhyme\\\" appears frequently,—appealing, indeed, to an\\nunrecognized sense more elusive than hearing.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Emily Dickinson scrutinized everything with clear-eyed frankness.\\nEvery subject was proper ground for legitimate study, even the\\nsombre facts of death and burial, and the unknown life beyond. She\\ntouches these themes sometimes lightly, sometimes almost\\nhumorously, more often with weird and peculiar power; but she is\\nnever by any chance frivolous or trivial. And while, as one critic\\nhas said, she may exhibit toward God \\\"an Emersonian self-possession,\\\"\\nit was because she looked upon all life with a candor as unprejudiced\\nas it is rare.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"She had tried society and the world, and found them lacking. She\\nwas not an invalid, and she lived in seclusion from no\\nlove-disappointment. Her life was the normal blossoming of a nature\\nintrospective to a high degree, whose best thought could not exist\\nin pretence.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Storm, wind, the wild March sky, sunsets and dawns; the birds and\\nbees, butterflies and flowers of her garden, with a few trusted\\nhuman friends, were sufficient companionship. The coming of the\\nfirst robin was a jubilee beyond crowning of monarch or birthday of\\npope; the first red leaf hurrying through \\\"the altered air,\\\" an\\nepoch. Immortality was close about her; and while never morbid or\\nmelancholy, she lived in its presence.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"MABEL LOOMIS TODD.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"AMHERST, MASSACHUSETTS,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"August, 1891.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"My nosegays are for captives;\\n Dim, long-expectant eyes,\\nFingers denied the plucking,\\n Patient till paradise,\\n\\nTo such, if they should whisper\\n Of morning and the moor,\\nThey bear no other errand,\\n And I, no other prayer.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I. LIFE.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I\'m nobody! Who are you?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Are you nobody, too?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Then there \'s a pair of us — don\'t tell!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"They \'d banish us, you know.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"How dreary to be somebody!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"How public, like a frog\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"To tell your name the livelong day\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"To an admiring bog!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"II.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I bring an unaccustomed wine\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"To lips long parching, next to mine,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And summon them to drink.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Crackling with fever, they essay;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I turn my brimming eyes away,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And come next hour to look.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The hands still hug the tardy glass;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The lips I would have cooled, alas!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Are so superfluous cold,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I would as soon attempt to warm\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The bosoms where the frost has lain\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Ages beneath the mould.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Some other thirsty there may be\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"To whom this would have pointed me\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Had it remained to speak.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And so I always bear the cup\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"If, haply, mine may be the drop\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Some pilgrim thirst to slake, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"If, haply, any say to me,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"\\\"Unto the little, unto me,\\\"\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"When I at last awake.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"III.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The nearest dream recedes, unrealized.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The heaven we chase\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Like the June bee\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Before the school-boy\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Invites the race;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Stoops to an easy clover —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Dips — evades — teases — deploys;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Then to the royal clouds\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Lifts his light pinnace\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Heedless of the boy\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Staring, bewildered, at the mocking sky.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Homesick for steadfast honey,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Ah! the bee flies not\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That brews that rare variety.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"IV.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"We play at paste,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Till qualified for pearl,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Then drop the paste,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And deem ourself a fool.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The shapes, though, were similar,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And our new hands\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Learned gem-tactics\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Practising sands.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"V.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I found the phrase to every thought\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I ever had, but one;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And that defies me, — as a hand\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Did try to chalk the sun\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"To races nurtured in the dark; —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"How would your own begin?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Can blaze be done in cochineal,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Or noon in mazarin?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"VI.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"HOPE.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Hope is the thing with feathers\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That perches in the soul,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And sings the tune without the words,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And never stops at all,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And sweetest in the gale is heard;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And sore must be the storm\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That could abash the little bird\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That kept so many warm.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I \'ve heard it in the chillest land,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And on the strangest sea;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Yet, never, in extremity,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"It asked a crumb of me.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"VII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"THE WHITE HEAT.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Dare you see a soul at the white heat?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Then crouch within the door.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Red is the fire\'s common tint;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But when the vivid ore\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Has sated flame\'s conditions,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Its quivering substance plays\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Without a color but the light\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Of unanointed blaze.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Least village boasts its blacksmith,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Whose anvil\'s even din\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Stands symbol for the finer forge\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That soundless tugs within,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Refining these impatient ores\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"With hammer and with blaze,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Until the designated light\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Repudiate the forge.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"VIII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"TRIUMPHANT.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Who never lost, are unprepared\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A coronet to find;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Who never thirsted, flagons\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And cooling tamarind.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Who never climbed the weary league —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Can such a foot explore\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The purple territories\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"On Pizarro\'s shore?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"How many legions overcome?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The emperor will say.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"How many colors taken\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"On Revolution Day?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"How many bullets bearest?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The royal scar hast thou?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Angels, write \\\"Promoted\\\"\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"On this soldier\'s brow!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"IX.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"THE TEST.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I can wade grief,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Whole pools of it, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I \'m used to that.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But the least push of joy\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Breaks up my feet,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And I tip — drunken.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Let no pebble smile,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"\'T was the new liquor, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That was all!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Power is only pain,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Stranded, through discipline,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Till weights will hang.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Give balm to giants,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And they \'ll wilt, like men.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Give Himmaleh, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"They \'ll carry him!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"X.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"ESCAPE.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I never hear the word \\\"escape\\\"\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Without a quicker blood,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A sudden expectation,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A flying attitude.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I never hear of prisons broad\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"By soldiers battered down,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But I tug childish at my bars, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Only to fail again!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XI.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"COMPENSATION.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"For each ecstatic instant\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"We must an anguish pay\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"In keen and quivering ratio\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"To the ecstasy.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"For each beloved hour\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Sharp pittances of years,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Bitter contested farthings\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And coffers heaped with tears.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"THE MARTYRS.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Through the straight pass of suffering\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The martyrs even trod,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Their feet upon temptation,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Their faces upon God.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A stately, shriven company;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Convulsion playing round,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Harmless as streaks of meteor\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Upon a planet\'s bound.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Their faith the everlasting troth;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Their expectation fair;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The needle to the north degree\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Wades so, through polar air.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XIII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A PRAYER.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I meant to have but modest needs,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Such as content, and heaven;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Within my income these could lie,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And life and I keep even.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But since the last included both,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"It would suffice my prayer\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But just for one to stipulate,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And grace would grant the pair.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And so, upon this wise I prayed, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Great Spirit, give to me\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A heaven not so large as yours,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But large enough for me.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A smile suffused Jehovah\'s face;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The cherubim withdrew;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Grave saints stole out to look at me,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And showed their dimples, too.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I left the place with all my might, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"My prayer away I threw;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The quiet ages picked it up,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And Judgment twinkled, too,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That one so honest be extant\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"As take the tale for true\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That \\\"Whatsoever you shall ask,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Itself be given you.\\\"\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But I, grown shrewder, scan the skies\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"With a suspicious air, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"As children, swindled for the first,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"All swindlers be, infer.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XIV.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The thought beneath so slight a film\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Is more distinctly seen, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"As laces just reveal the surge,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Or mists the Apennine.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XV.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The soul unto itself\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Is an imperial friend, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Or the most agonizing spy\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"An enemy could send.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Secure against its own,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"No treason it can fear;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Itself its sovereign, of itself\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The soul should stand in awe.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XVI.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Surgeons must be very careful\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"When they take the knife!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Underneath their fine incisions\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Stirs the culprit, — Life!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XVII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"THE RAILWAY TRAIN.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I like to see it lap the miles,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And lick the valleys up,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And stop to feed itself at tanks;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And then, prodigious, step\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Around a pile of mountains,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And, supercilious, peer\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"In shanties by the sides of roads;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And then a quarry pare\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"To fit its sides, and crawl between,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Complaining all the while\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"In horrid, hooting stanza;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Then chase itself down hill\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And neigh like Boanerges;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Then, punctual as a star,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Stop — docile and omnipotent —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"At its own stable door.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XVIII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"THE SHOW.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The show is not the show,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But they that go.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Menagerie to me\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"My neighbor be.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Fair play —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Both went to see.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XIX.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Delight becomes pictorial\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"When viewed through pain, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"More fair, because impossible\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That any gain.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The mountain at a given distance\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"In amber lies;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Approached, the amber flits a little, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And that \'s the skies!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XX.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A thought went up my mind to-day\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That I have had before,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But did not finish, — some way back,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I could not fix the year,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Nor where it went, nor why it came\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The second time to me,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Nor definitely what it was,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Have I the art to say.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But somewhere in my soul, I know\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I \'ve met the thing before;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"It just reminded me — \'t was all —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And came my way no more.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXI.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Is Heaven a physician?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"They say that He can heal,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But medicine posthumous\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Is unavailable.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Is Heaven an exchequer?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"They speak of what we owe;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But that negotiation\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I \'m not a party to.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"THE RETURN.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Though I get home how late, how late!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"So I get home, \'t will compensate.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Better will be the ecstasy\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That they have done expecting me,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"When, night descending, dumb and dark,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"They hear my unexpected knock.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Transporting must the moment be,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Brewed from decades of agony!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"To think just how the fire will burn,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Just how long-cheated eyes will turn\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"To wonder what myself will say,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And what itself will say to me,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Beguiles the centuries of way!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXIII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A poor torn heart, a tattered heart,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That sat it down to rest,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Nor noticed that the ebbing day\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Flowed silver to the west,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Nor noticed night did soft descend\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Nor constellation burn,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Intent upon the vision\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Of latitudes unknown.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The angels, happening that way,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"This dusty heart espied;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Tenderly took it up from toil\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And carried it to God.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"There, — sandals for the barefoot;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"There, — gathered from the gales,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Do the blue havens by the hand\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Lead the wandering sails.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXIV.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"TOO MUCH.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I should have been too glad, I see,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Too lifted for the scant degree\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Of life\'s penurious round;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"My little circuit would have shamed\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"This new circumference, have blamed\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The homelier time behind.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I should have been too saved, I see,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Too rescued; fear too dim to me\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That I could spell the prayer\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I knew so perfect yesterday, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That scalding one, \\\"Sabachthani,\\\"\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Recited fluent here.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Earth would have been too much, I see,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And heaven not enough for me;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I should have had the joy\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Without the fear to justify, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The palm without the Calvary;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"So, Saviour, crucify.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Defeat whets victory, they say;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The reefs in old Gethsemane\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Endear the shore beyond.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"\'T is beggars banquets best define;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"\'T is thirsting vitalizes wine, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Faith faints to understand.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXV.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"SHIPWRECK.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"It tossed and tossed, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A little brig I knew, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"O\'ertook by blast,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"It spun and spun,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And groped delirious, for morn.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"It slipped and slipped,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"As one that drunken stepped;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Its white foot tripped,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Then dropped from sight.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Ah, brig, good-night\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"To crew and you;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The ocean\'s heart too smooth, too blue,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"To break for you.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXVI.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Victory comes late,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And is held low to freezing lips\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Too rapt with frost\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"To take it.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"How sweet it would have tasted,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Just a drop!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Was God so economical?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"His table \'s spread too high for us\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Unless we dine on tip-toe.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Crumbs fit such little mouths,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Cherries suit robins;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The eagle\'s golden breakfast\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Strangles them.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"God keeps his oath to sparrows,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Who of little love\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Know how to starve!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXVII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"ENOUGH.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"God gave a loaf to every bird,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But just a crumb to me;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I dare not eat it, though I starve, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"My poignant luxury\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"To own it, touch it, prove the feat\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That made the pellet mine, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Too happy in my sparrow chance\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"For ampler coveting.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"It might be famine all around,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I could not miss an ear,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Such plenty smiles upon my board,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"My garner shows so fair.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I wonder how the rich may feel, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"An Indiaman — an Earl?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I deem that I with but a crumb\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Am sovereign of them all.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXVIII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Experiment to me\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Is every one I meet.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"If it contain a kernel?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The figure of a nut\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Presents upon a tree,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Equally plausibly;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But meat within is requisite,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"To squirrels and to me.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXIX.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"MY COUNTRY\'S WARDROBE.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"My country need not change her gown,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Her triple suit as sweet\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"As when \'t was cut at Lexington,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And first pronounced \\\"a fit.\\\"\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Great Britain disapproves \\\"the stars;\\\"\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Disparagement discreet, —\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"There \'s something in their attitude\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"That taunts her bayonet.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXX.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Faith is a fine invention\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"For gentlemen who see;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But microscopes are prudent\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"In an emergency!\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXXI.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Except the heaven had come so near,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"So seemed to choose my door,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The distance would not haunt me so;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I had not hoped before.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But just to hear the grace depart\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I never thought to see,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Afflicts me with a double loss;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"\'T is lost, and lost to me.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXXII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Portraits are to daily faces\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"As an evening west\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"To a fine, pedantic sunshine\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"In a satin vest.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXXIII.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"THE DUEL.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I took my power in my hand.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"And went against the world;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"\'T was not so much as David had,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"But I was twice as bold.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"I aimed my pebble, but myself\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Was all the one that fell.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Was it Goliath was too large,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Or only I too small?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"XXXIV.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"A shady friend for torrid days\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Is easier to find\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Than one of higher temperature\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"For frigid hour of mind.\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"The vane a little to the east\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Scares muslin souls away;\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"If broadcloth breasts are firmer\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Than those of organdy,\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Who is to blame? The weaver?\"},{\"heading\":false,\"text\":\"Ah! the bewildering thread!\"},{\"heading\":false